WEBVTT

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:10.927
Hi there.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:15.535
Welcome to this video where we are going
to learn about strong and weak passwords.

00:00:16.095 --> 00:00:21.135
In this video you will learn why some
passwords are safe and others are risky.

00:00:21.935 --> 00:00:28.127
Understanding this helps
keep your digital identity secure.

00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:34.703
Passwords exist to protect 
accounts from other people.

00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:38.223
They act like a secret key
that only the real user should know.

00:00:39.295 --> 00:00:42.703
When passwords are weak,
this protection does not work well.

00:00:43.023 --> 00:00:46.015
That is why password's strength matters.

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.815
A weak password is easy to guess.

00:00:52.815 --> 00:00:57.167
It often uses short words, 
simple numbers, or personal information.

00:00:58.127 --> 00:01:01.935
Attackers try these passwords first
because they are very common.

00:01:02.607 --> 00:01:05.615
Weak passwords make attacks fast and easy.

00:01:06.255 --> 00:01:10.895
Examples of weak passwords
include "1234", "password"

00:01:10.895 --> 00:01:12.895
or your own name.

00:01:12.895 --> 00:01:16.463
Birthdays, pet names,
and favorite teams are also risky.

00:01:17.183 --> 00:01:20.383
These details are easy 
for others to find or guess.

00:01:21.055 --> 00:01:23.535
Using them makes accounts unsafe.

00:01:24.495 --> 00:01:27.743
Attackers use computer programs
to guess passwords.

00:01:27.855 --> 00:01:31.423
These programs can try
thousands of passwords very quickly.

00:01:31.903 --> 00:01:34.575
Weak passwords are often
guessed in seconds.

00:01:34.575 --> 00:01:37.583
Imagine if the password contains
two different digits.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:41.343
There are only 90 combinations
of the password, and computers

00:01:41.343 --> 00:01:43.247
would find it very quickly.

00:01:43.247 --> 00:01:46.399
This is why it is important
to have a strong password.

00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:49.791
A strong password is hard to guess.

00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:52.719
It does not include personal information.

00:01:52.719 --> 00:01:56.079
It is long and uses
a mix of different characters.

00:01:56.879 --> 00:01:59.887
Strong passwords slow attackers down.

00:02:00.095 --> 00:02:04.335
Strong passwords use letters, 
numbers, and symbols together.

00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:07.775
They are usually longer
than simple passwords.

00:02:07.775 --> 00:02:10.943
The more variety and length, 
the safer the password is.

00:02:11.535 --> 00:02:14.543
This makes guessing much harder.

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:21.631
Using the same password
for many accounts is risky.

00:02:22.079 --> 00:02:25.839
If one account is hacked, attackers
can try that password everywhere.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.471
This can lead to many accounts
being taken over.

00:02:29.759 --> 00:02:32.751
Reuse increases the damage of one mistake.

00:02:32.991 --> 00:02:35.791
Sometimes online systems 
such as ticket booking systems

00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:38.799
are hacked and passwords are stolen.

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:42.718
If you reuse passwords, attackers
can unlock other accounts too.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.718
This is why each account
should have a different password.

00:02:47.278 --> 00:02:49.598
Unique passwords limit the risk.

00:02:49.598 --> 00:02:51.310
Passwords should never be shared

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.558
with anyone, not with friends, 
classmates, or strangers.

00:02:55.198 --> 00:02:58.670
Sharing passwords breaks 
account protection completely.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:02.238
Secrets only work when they stay secret.

00:03:02.878 --> 00:03:06.030
Writing passwords on paper 
or notes can be risky.

00:03:06.558 --> 00:03:09.470
Others may find them or take photos.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:12.478
This can lead to accounts 
being accessed without permission.

00:03:13.038 --> 00:03:15.598
Safer solutions exist.

00:03:15.598 --> 00:03:18.590
Strong and unique
passwords can be hard to remember.

00:03:19.182 --> 00:03:22.222
This makes people tempted 
to choose weak passwords.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.710
Remembering many passwords 
is a real challenge.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.342
That is why tools can help.

00:03:28.766 --> 00:03:32.686
There is a tool that helps 
manage many strong passwords safely.

00:03:32.782 --> 00:03:35.422
This tool is called a password manager.

00:03:35.422 --> 00:03:38.414
It helps avoid weak passwords and reuse.

00:03:43.182 --> 00:03:46.174
Weak passwords are 
easy to guess and risky.

00:03:47.054 --> 00:03:48.862
Strong passwords are long,

00:03:48.862 --> 00:03:51.854
unique, and hard to guess.

00:03:51.918 --> 00:03:55.038
Good password choices
protect digital identity.

00:03:55.726 --> 00:03:58.718
Strength really matters.

00:03:59.614 --> 00:04:01.182
Thank you for watching.

00:04:01.182 --> 00:04:04.142
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.